@startuml Implementation_View
title Smart E-Mobility Hub — Development / Implementation View (Submission 3)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 45

package "Presentation" {
  [Student Portal] as StudentUI
  [Operator Portal] as OperatorUI
}

package "Application and domain modules" as Modules {
  package "Operational modules" as Operational {
    [Hub & Identity] as Hub
    [Vehicle Rental] as Rental
    [Parking & Private EV] as Parking
    [Fleet & Incident] as Fleet
    [Smart Charging] as Charging
  }
  [What-if Simulation] as Simulation
}

package "Shared contracts and adapters" as Shared {
  [API handlers / role checks] as API
  [Snapshot contract] as Snapshot
  [Repository contracts] as Repository
  [JSON / in-memory adapter] as DataAdapter
  [Telemetry intake adapter] as Telemetry
}

StudentUI --> API : student requests
OperatorUI --> API : operator requests
API --> Modules : route authorized requests
API --> Hub : authenticate
Rental --> Hub : Hub availability
Rental --> Parking : return capacity
Parking --> Hub : status / alternatives
Parking --> Charging : submit / read / cancel\nrequests or stop charging
Charging --> Parking : linked parking window\nand eligibility
Fleet --> Parking : validated occupancy
Fleet --> Rental : vehicle restrictions
Fleet --> Charging : point faults
Telemetry --> Fleet : verified observations
Simulation --> Snapshot : read versioned state
Snapshot --> Operational : read all five providers
Modules --> Repository : load / save module state
Repository --> DataAdapter : persistence adapter

note bottom of Simulation
  Each run works on a copied snapshot;
  recommendations do not change live operations.
end note
@enduml
